WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.634
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're talking to one of

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:03.734
our favorites, the one and only
Tyler Perry.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.167
Come on now.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:09.767
I want to talk about your new
movie, "A Jazzman's Blues."

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.234
You wrote and directed the this.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.267
It's getting great reviews,
by the way.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.767
-Can you imagine a Tyler Perry
movie getting great reviews?

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.067
-Yeah.
What is that like for you?

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.601
Do you go like --
Do you read the reviews?

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.133
-I never read them.
I haven't read them in the past.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.601
But Oprah called me up.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.400
She said, "Tyler, have you read
the review from 'Variety'?"

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.701
I was like, "No."
She said, "No, no, no,

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.667
you need to read it."
I was like, "No, I don't want to

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.834
open that in my mind."
She was like, "No, no, no."

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.033
And she -- I was like, "No."
She's like, "Okay."

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.701
So she starts reading it to me
on the phone.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.334
-Yeah. If it's Oprah,
what are you going to say?

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:38.467
-You got to listen to it.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.834
You want Oprah to read anything
to you.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.367
-Anything to you at all, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.501
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.234
-It is fantastic.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.834
You got to see this movie.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.968
The story behind it is
even cooler.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.901
This is a screenplay
that you wrote 27 years ago.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:51.901
-27 years ago. Yeah.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.801
26 years old, broke, struggling.

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:57.267
And I snuck into a play,
a theater in Atlanta

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.133
called the Alliance Theatre,
and August Wilson was having

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:00.467
a play called
"Two Trains Running."

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.934
-August Wilson?
-Yeah, and I got a chance

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.634
to talk to him,
and I had nothing,

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.200
and he was really encouraging.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.834
And he told me to go write
what was in my heart.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.701
And I went home and "Jazzman"
started to pour out then.

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:11.501
-Yeah. And did you think that

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.801
you were going to be
in the movie?

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.467
-Yeah, well, I had big dreams
even though I was broke.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.701
Yeah, I wanted to be the lead.
Nobody knew my name.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:22.200
But I wanted Will Smith
to play the co-lead.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.067
Diana Ross, Halle Berry,

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:26.567
I wanted all these people
in the movie.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.934
-Wow.
-But I aged out.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.901
'Cause it starts
when he's 17 years old,

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:35.901
and even though I try to look
my best, I can't pull off 17.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.834
Not even with digital Botox
you can't pull that off.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.400
[ Laughter ]
So I found an incredible cast.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.701
And Debbie Allen
did the choreography

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.267
and Terry Fletcher
did the music.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:46.100
-I love Debbie Allen.
-It's really phenomenal.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.234
-Can you tell everyone
what the film is about?

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:51.133
-It's about two star-crossed
lovers who find themselves

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:54.033
in very difficult situations,
set in the 1940s,

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.801
and all these obstacles
against them,

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.434
trying to keep their love apart.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.667
But no matter what happens,

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.634
they always seem to find
each other again.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.934
So it's a powerful,
powerful film.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.501
-Yeah, it's beautiful.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.100
Here's a scene from Tyler
Perry's "A Jazzman's Blues."

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.467
Take a look at this.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:13.367
[ Jazz music playing ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:17.601
-♪ Let the good times roll ♪

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.701
♪ Don't carry your load ♪

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:24.000
♪ Get together and let
the good times roll ♪

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.200
♪♪

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.901
♪ No matter what, it's rainy
weather, birds of a feather ♪

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:35.434
♪ Got to stick together ♪

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.501
♪ So get yourself
under control ♪

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:41.300
♪ Go out and get together
and let the good times roll ♪

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.567
♪♪

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:45.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.434
-How y'all doing?
Y'all alright?

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.767
-I mean, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.934
It's a different --
-Totally different.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:58.400
-It's a departure for you, but I
love that you keep doing this.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.934
And this is the one that
kind of got you started.

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:03.167
This is -- Congrats on
the fantastic reviews.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.801
Who are those --
There's some new faces there.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.100
-Amirah Vann.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.968
Austin Scott was in that clip.
And Milauna Jackson.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:12.734
And Solea Pfeiffer and Joshua
Boone, they lead the movie.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.434
And all new faces that are
incredibly talented

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.501
that I'm excited about.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:17.567
-Thank you for
doing all this stuff.

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:18.801
And, dude,
congrats on everything.

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:20.434
-Thank you.
-It's a great movie.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.734
Tyler Perry, everybody.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.968
"A Jazzman's Blues" premieres
tomorrow on Netflix.

